  "summary": "The V1 approach in the instructions is well-scoped and practical. The single integration point in move_to_stage() when stage=='done' is the right call — it's already the canonical transition point and currently has no side effects, so adding a synchronous file-append there is clean and low-risk. For the capture mechanism, mechanical extraction should pull from the feature JSON's 'plan' field (which contains the approved plan summary), 'impl_notes' (if populated), and any review feedback entries. The key implementation detail is formatting these raw fields into concise bullet points without an LLM — the simplest approach is to extract the first 2-3 sentences of each field and present them under labeled sub-headers (Decisions, Patterns, Gotchas), accepting that some entries will be more useful than others and relying on manual curation to prune low-value ones. For context inclusion, read_board_context_file(config, board) in config.py should mirror read_context_file() exactly but with a 30KB cap and board-specific path (.mad/boards/<board>/BOARD_CONTEXT.md). In _prepend_context() in runner.py, the board name needs to be passed through — the runner already has access to the feature's board via the FeatureFile object, so threading this through is straightforward. The V1 restriction to planning and implementation stages (not review) is pragmatic and avoids the stage-filtering complexity that stalled prior rounds. The 30KB cap with a TUI warning is sufficient size management — no automatic summarization needed."
